<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<exercise xml:id="exercise-comparison-of-topologies-on-r" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>
    Comparison of topologies on <m> \R </m>
  </title>
  
  <statement>
    <p>
      Compare the following topologies on the real numbers <m> \R </m>: the indiscrete topology <m> \bot_{ \R } </m>; the discrete topology <m> \top_{ \R } </m>; the Euclidean topology <m> \tau_{ d } </m>; the cofinite topology <m> \tau_{ 1 } </m>; the cocountable topology <m> \tau_{ 2 } </m>; the particular point topology <m> \tau_{ 3 } </m> specified with particular point <m> 0 \in \R </m>; and the excluded point topology <m> \tau_{ 4 } </m> specified with excluded point <m> 0 \in \R </m>.
    </p>
  </statement>
  
  <answer>
    <p>
      We observe that all comparison relationships can be summarized by
      
      <md>
        <mrow>
          \bot_{ \R } \amp \subseteq \tau_{ 1 } \subseteq \tau_{ 2 } \subseteq \top_{ \R }
        </mrow>
        
        <mrow>
          \bot_{ \R } \amp \subseteq \tau_{ 1 } \subseteq \tau_{ d } \subseteq \top_{ \R }
        </mrow>
        
        <mrow>
          \bot_{ \R } \amp \subseteq \tau_{ 3 } \subseteq \top_{ \R }
        </mrow>
        
        <mrow>
          \bot_{ \R } \amp \subseteq \tau_{ 4 } \subseteq \top_{ \R }
        </mrow>
      </md>.
    </p>
  </answer>
</exercise>
